    fix(rtl-math): isolate math expressions in Persian RTL text — root-cause display-layer fix (P0 owner mission)
    
    Problem: Persian-digit numbers (bidi EN) render as separate runs and neutral
    operators (× ÷ = < >) take RTL direction, visually scrambling expressions —
    «۱۰−۲×۳» displayed as «۳ × ۱۰−۲» (proven via Range-API geometric measurements:
    3@x993 left of 10@x1081). Second, inverse defect: ltr-nums applied to word-mixed
    formulaBox strings scrambled PERSIAN WORD ORDER (جمله separated from its suffix).
    
    Root fix (display layer only — no data/logic/content changes, no manual glyph
    reordering, no data re-ordering to compensate bidi):
    - src/utils/mathBidi.ts: conservative math-segment detector (operator between
      digits | leading sign | balanced parens w/ digit; Persian-letter runs break;
      trailing-sign convention «۳−»/«(۲−)», lone numbers, fractions ۳/۴, decimals,
      percents and «۲³» deliberately NOT isolated; sentence-final dot returns to RTL)
    - src/components/MathText.tsx: renders math segments as <span dir="ltr"
      class="math-iso"> (dir attribute + unicode-bidi:isolate) inside unchanged RTL
      text; Persian digits preserved byte-for-byte
    - index.css: .math-iso (no inline-block) alongside legacy .ltr-nums
    - Applied at 54 render points across 11 files: QuestionCard (prompt/options/
      hints/explanation/feedback/diagnosis/review), LessonFlowPlayer (narrative/
      scenario/remedial/representations/worked-example×4/finalAnswer/completion/
      sequencing labels+hint), StepSolverAnimation (captions/finish/mistake),
      InteractiveLabs (cylinder 2 lines), ProtoShared (ProtoHeader+DotModel caption+
      ResultChip label — central for A/B/C), PrototypeA (choice buttons/feedbacks/
      hint/summary), PrototypeB (2 chips/hints/flash/B3/B4 feedbacks), PrototypeC
      (ladder/guided/transfer prompt+options+feedback), App (formulaBox — fixes
      category B — + dashboard diagnoses), AssistantPanel (reply text)
    
    Tests: new tests/mathBidiRendering.test.tsx — 40 tests covering all 9 owner
    edge expressions (۱۰−۲×۳ / ۵+(۶×۲)−(۴÷۲) / −۸+۳ / ۱۲÷۳=۴ / ۱٫۵+۲٫۵ / ۳/۴+۱/۴ /
    ۲³ / ۵<۸ / (۲، ۳)): exact content preservation + correct isolation + conservative
    non-isolation rules + QuestionCard central rendering. Updated 3 existing test
    matchers (app.test, flowOperationOrder) for node-fragmentation-tolerant queries —
    behavior assertions unchanged.
    
    Gates (audit/rtl-math/gates/): tsc 0, eslint 0, vitest 386/386 (346 existing +
    40 new), F06-F10 regression 49/49, vite build OK (index-CksJxeIp.js
    3ff293e7…), browser console 0 errors across all before/after runs.
    
    Evidence: audit/rtl-math/{AUDIT.md,REPORT.md} + 12 real before-shots +
    12 real after-shots (desktop 1280 + mobile 390, real dev-server runs) +
    Range-API visual-order before/after JSONs — after-measurements prove standard
    LTR math order inside RTL text and restored Persian word order in formulaBox.
    
    Owner-decision items (NOT changed): ch1 trailing-sign data convention «۳−»,
    ch1:287 «۵− + ۸ = ۳+» data order, speed-label «۰/۵×» convention. NOT VERIFIED:
    real-device touch, full screen-reader session, non-Chromium browsers.
    
    Git: work branch prototypes/interactive-learning only, NO push/merge/deploy;
    backup bundle download/ryazi-yar-six-pre-rtl-math-fix-20261101.bundle; main and
    origin/main untouched at 77a5a38. Stop-point: awaiting owner review.

